# With fifty-two guests in Russian: numbers in every case
subtitle: "С пятью гостями, для двадцати человек, о трёх салатах: how Russian numbers change in every case, and the noun with them."
tags: ["russian","russian numbers","numbers in cases","с пятью","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/numerals-in-cases","vocabulary/kitchen"]
thumb: "band \"Numbers change too\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"We all got together in Russian: собрались, разошлись","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/165-russian-gathered.cast"}

